[2026-09-03T18:01:12Z] ADDED per-GPU VRAM tracking (main.py + gpu.py + system/index.js + index.html + styles.css): each GPU gets its own graph + toggle; untracked GPUs (e.g. iGPU) are excluded from the aggregate total; tracked state persisted in .metallama_gpu_config.json (excluded_gpus list, default = all tracked). New endpoints: GET /api/system/vram/gpus, POST /api/system/vram/gpus/toggle; /api/system/vram/history now returns per-GPU history under 'gpus'. Also FIXED gpu.py tool detection under systemd's restricted PATH (venv-only): added absolute-path fallbacks for rocm-smi/amd-smi and made query functions use the resolved tool path. VERIFIED end-to-end in browser: toggle card2 off drops aggregate 48.5→48.0 GB, persists across reload, re-enable restores.
